---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const title = "Disclaimer | PaintingPricing Calculator";
const description = "What PaintingPricing Calculator's estimates are, and aren't — read this before quoting a real customer.";
---

<LegalLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  heading="Disclaimer"
  updated="September 17, 2026"
>
  <section>
    <p>
      This page explains what PaintingPricing Calculator's numbers actually
      are, so there's no confusion between "a calculation based on what you
      typed in" and "professional advice you can rely on without checking
      it." Please read it before using any figure from this tool in a real
      quote to a real customer.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Estimates only — not a guarantee</h2>
    <p>
      Every number the Site produces — cost, price, margin, paint/material
      quantities, labor hours — is a calculation based entirely on the
      values you enter. It is an estimate, not a guarantee of your actual
      costs, the outcome of any specific job, or your resulting profit.
      Actual material usage, labor time, waste, and site conditions can and
      do differ from any estimate.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on the Site is financial, accounting, tax, legal, or
      contracting advice. It's a calculation aid built around the formulas
      and inputs you provide — it doesn't know your local market rates,
      your business's real overhead, your contracts, or your obligations
      under any law or licensing requirement that applies to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sample figures are illustrative only</h2>
    <p>
      Any example prices, rates, or margins shown on the Site (including
      on the homepage and in the Pro preview) are illustrative examples of
      how the tool works — they are not recommended market rates and
      shouldn't be used as a benchmark for what to charge.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>You decide what to charge</h2>
    <p>
      The Site shows you how a proposed price relates to your entered
      costs and target margin. It does not, and is not meant to, tell you
      what to charge a customer. That decision — and the responsibility for
      it — is entirely yours.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Garbage in, garbage out</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculation is only as accurate as the numbers you put in. If
      your material costs, labor rates, or measurements are wrong or
      out of date, the resulting estimate will be too. Always double-check
      your inputs, and re-verify any figure before putting it in front of
      a customer.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>No liability for business outcomes</h2>
    <p>
      We aren't responsible for losses, disputes with your customers,
      underbid jobs, or any other business outcome that results from
      relying on a number this Site produced. See the{" "}
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for the full limitation of
      liability.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about how a calculation works? <a href="/contact">Get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
